  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 134 AM CDT Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nMore tranquil weather expected for Wednesday with slightly warmer \nthan normal temperatures and light winds. Models then show a weaker \nshortwave coming out of the central Rockies into the Plains \nWednesday night and Thursday. A few showers may occur on Thursday, \nbut the models show the wave weakening as it moves across the area. \nMay end up with mainly an increase in clouds across the northern \nhalf of the area during the day, cooling temperatures there by a \ndegree or two from previous day.  \n\nNorthwest flow then develops as we approach the weekend with the \npotential for a few shortwave diving south through the central and \nsouthern Plains. Model differences increase by this time with regards \nto the strength of these individual wave and the potential for \nadditional precip chances.",
